 *   **Limitations**: Requires more kernels than 3DGS to achieve comparable or better results, increasing memory usage [S1].
 
 ## Background
-3D Half-Gaussian Splatting (3D-HGS) was introduced in the paper "3D-HGS: 3D Half-Gaussian Splatting" [S1]. It extends the 3D Gaussian Splatting framework by using half-ellipsoids to represent surfaces, which are more suitable for modeling sharp boundaries and occlusions than full ellipsoids. The method was evaluated against Scaffold, mip-splatting, and MCMC architectures [S1].
